\viewkind4\uc1\pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\ulnone\b0 
\par 1.  I always die, because death is near;\cf0 
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 My life draws near the grave daily.
\par There is none whose life is in his hand,
\par And cannot foretell the future.
\par Time is running fast, death is near,
\par Oh who possesses such knowledge?
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par  2.  It is only the sinful person,
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 That remains and dies in his sin.
\par It is only the infested tree,
\par That weakens and falls in no time.
\par The death unnoticed and hidden,
\par Is located in the body.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\qj\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3.   As for death, it comes but unannounced,
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 It occurs unexpectedly.
\par It takes men into new domicile,
\par To render accounts on their deeds.
\par Either good living or troubles,
\par All happen after death of man.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\qj\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par  4.  Oh King of Kings, and Lord of all Lords,
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0\qj In Thy hand is our life and death.
\par What Thou grants us is What comes to pass,
\par For us, we agree to Thy will.
\par Let me always remember this,
\par So that I diligently watch.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5.  A little downfall just like this one,
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0\qj Can bring my life to abrupt end.
\par Oh my Lord, now let me hold Thy hand,
\par Watch Jesus' interceding death.
\par During the death of my body,
\par Let my spirit clinch unto Him.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6.  If I'm not able to say a word,
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 And unable to think ahead.
\par At that time, this is what I will say:
\par 'Lord, kindly receive my spirit'.
\par If I shut my mouth and keep mute,
\par Let the blood of Jesus save me.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\qj\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 7\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 7.  Even when I'm scared by the end time,
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 Please, open heaven's gate for me.
\par Oh then break the strains of death for me,
\par Then draw me nearer to Thy side.
\par My parting will bother no one,
\par \pard    Rather it will give only rest.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2\fs14 
\par }

